  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S039",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, good to meet you too. So, man, it’s... it’s a lot, honestly. I’ve been trying to figure out how to explain it because usually I’m really on top of things, you know? I’m an electrician, and in my line of work, you’ve gotta be sharp. But lately... well, what finally pushed me to make this appointment, what finally got me into this chair today, is that I just cannot, for the life of me, keep my focus on a single estimate or a code form anymore. \n\nAnd those forms are crucial, right? You mess up a code compliance form and you’re looking at failed inspections, which costs money, delays the whole project, and makes you look bad to the general contractors. But I’ll be sitting there at my desk in the shop, trying to run the numbers, and then—bam—I hear a tool noise out in the bay. Like, the air compressor kicks on, or someone drops a pair of wire strippers, and my brain just completely snaps to that. Or my phone buzzes with a text, and I have to look, and then suddenly I’m not even thinking about the text anymore because I’m thinking about this massive new idea I have for reorganizing the entire workshop. Like, building these custom shelving units for the conduit and the breakers, which is a brilliant idea, don't get me wrong, I've got the whole schematic mapped out in my head...\n\nBut the problem is, I get completely pulled off track from the paperwork I was supposed to be doing. Hours go by, I’ve started three other things, and then the jobs start getting all mixed up. I’m putting the materials for a residential job onto the invoice for a downtown office reno, and it’s just... it’s a disaster. I’ve never been this scattered before, and it’s really starting to mess with my livelihood and my reputation, so I figured I had to come in and talk to somebody about it because I can't keep operating like this, it's just not sustainable.",
