    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "When you’re feeling this revved up, do you need less sleep than usual?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S036",
      "patient_response": "Oh man, the sleep thing. That's actually one of the craziest parts of all this, because usually, I'm a solid eight-hours-a-night guy. You know, pulling wire and crawling through attics all day, it takes it out of you. You usually hit the mattress and you're out cold. But lately? For months now, honestly, I've been getting by on... I don't know, maybe three or four hours a night? Max. \n\nAnd the wild part is, I don't feel tired at all. Not even a little bit. I'll hit the pillow at maybe 1 or 2 AM because I'm just buzzing with all these ideas for the shop and the solar expansion, and then—bam—my eyes just snap open before dawn. It's like 4:30 in the morning and I am just wide awake, completely refreshed, like I just slept a full, deep ten hours. \n\nI'll literally pop out of bed, make a pot of coffee that I don't even really need because I'm already wired, and I'm just instantly ready to go. I'll sit down at the kitchen table in the pitch black and start pricing out materials for the week—checking the current rates on copper, looking at PVC bulk pricing—and then I'm firing off emails to our suppliers and the general contractors before they're even awake. Or I'll be sketching out another whole system for that solar pitch I was telling you about, just drawing up the schematics, figuring out the inverter loads, right there at the breakfast table. It's like there just aren't enough hours in the day, so my brain just decided to stop needing sleep so I can get all this stuff done, you know? It feels incredibly productive, but then I look at the clock and it's 5 AM and I've already done half a day's work.",
