    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "When you’re feeling this revved up, have you had experiences where you believed things that other people said weren’t true or realistic?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S035",
      "patient_response": "Well, it’s funny you use the word 'realistic' because, yeah, I’ve been getting into some arguments with the guys at the shop about exactly that. Like, my boss, he thinks I'm getting way ahead of myself, and he's been pretty vocal about it. \n\nSee, lately I just have this... this overwhelming feeling that I am completely ready to take on these massive commercial jobs. And I'm not just talking about, you know, wiring up a little mom-and-pop storefront or changing out some fluorescent ballasts. I'm talking about bidding on these huge, multi-story office build-outs downtown. The real heavy-duty stuff. I keep telling everyone at the shop that we need to pivot right now, that I can handle the estimating, the project management, the whole nine yards. I even started putting together this whole training manual at my kitchen table at like 3 AM, because I feel like I could hire and train a whole new crew of apprentices right now. I just want to bring in like ten green guys and get them all up to speed in a week. I've got the whole curriculum laid out in my head—how I'd teach them complex conduit bending, three-phase systems, commercial load calculations, everything. \n\nAnd the guys at work, they're looking at me like I've lost my mind. They keep telling me it's impossible and that I'm not being realistic. And... I mean, I guess, if I really take a step back and force myself to look at it objectively, part of me knows they have a point. Like, I know my licensing and my actual years of experience aren’t quite where they need to be for all that yet. You need a master electrician's license to pull the permits for commercial jobs of that scale, and I'm still a journeyman. I still need a couple more years of logged hours before I can even sit for the master's exam. \n\nSo logically, somewhere in the back of my head, I know I don't have the credentials on paper to be running a ten-man crew on a high-rise. But when I'm in that zone? When my brain is just firing on all cylinders? I just look at the blueprints and I know, I absolutely know, that I can do it better than any master electrician in this city. I just feel like I'm completely ready for it, even if everyone else is telling me to pump the brakes.",
