      "doctor_question": "Have there been clear periods when you felt like this, separated by times when you were back to your usual self?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, see, that's the thing. It hasn't really been like an on-and-off switch lately. Usually, yeah, I'd have a week where I'm really fired up, maybe knock out a bunch of side jobs, and then I'd sort of settle back into my normal rhythm. You know, just regular old me, going to work, coming home, watching a little TV, getting a solid eight hours. \n\nBut this time? This time it's been different. It's been this constant, steady build. Like... like a pressure cooker that's just been slowly heating up and heating up. I'd say it's been going on for about seven months now. Just this relentless energy and all these massive ideas that just won't quit. \n\nAnd I can actually pinpoint exactly when it started, too. It was right around the time my business partner and I took out the mortgage for the new workshop and all the heavy equipment. We finally pulled the trigger on getting our own space, you know? We bought this great little commercial property out on Route 9, and we financed a couple of new work trucks, a scissor lift, some really high-end diagnostic gear... the whole setup. \n\nAnd man, the day we signed those papers, it was like someone flipped a switch in my brain. I just started thinking, 'Okay, we have the overhead now. We have the mortgage, we have the equipment loans, we need to hustle.' And that hustle just... it just never stopped. It just kept escalating. I started working longer hours, then the sleep started dropping off, then the ideas started getting bigger and bigger. So yeah, for the last seven months, since we took on all that debt for the shop, I haven't really had a break. I haven't gone back to my 'usual self' at all. It's just been this one, long, continuous upward climb, and I don't feel like I'm coming down anytime soon. I just feel like I'm gaining momentum, honestly.",
